<edge source="iran_us_regional_war::proxy_activation_level" target="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater proxy mobilization (missiles, drones, fast boats and interdictions) produces more direct strikes and interdictions against energy shipping and related maritime infrastructure, raising the measured frequency of attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_regional_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_us_regional_war::proxy_activation_level" target="market_monetary_stress::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Wider and more intense proxy fighting elevates perceived sovereign and regional risk, driving up term premia and long-dated government yields for exposed issuers as investors demand higher compensation for prolonged geopolitical risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_regional_war</data>
  <data key="d40">market_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_us_regional_war::proxy_activation_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::fuel_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened activation of Iran-backed proxies (e.g., Houthi attacks) against tankers and shipping lanes disrupts tanker transits and commercial schedules, directly reducing the volume and continuity of liquid fuel shipments reaching European and regional markets relevant to the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_regional_war</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_us_regional_war::proxy_activation_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_deployment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater activation of proxies increases demand for ISR, targeting, logistics and autonomous force‑multipliers, prompting militaries and defense contractors to accelerate procurement and fielding of AI systems and pushing some commercial operators to expedite AI deployment for continuity and resilience.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_us_regional_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
