  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">High frequency strikes on critical infrastructure and financial plumbing force central banks into repeated emergency interventions, ad‑hoc liquidity measures, or temporary controls that undermine markets' confidence in the bank's steady adherence to its price‑stability mandate.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">market_monetary_stress</data>
