</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::crude_price_level" target="iran_us_regional_war::proxy_activation_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained increase in crude prices raises export revenue for oil-dependent actors (including Iran), enabling greater financing, weapons procurement, and logistical support for regional proxies, thereby increasing their operational tempo and geographic reach.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_us_regional_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::crude_price_level" target="market_monetary_stress::inflation_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in crude prices directly increases consumer fuel and transport costs and upstream input prices, which market participants and survey respondents incorporate into near‑term and medium‑term inflation expectations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">market_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::crude_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_support_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in crude prices raise domestic energy and fiscal burdens in allied countries, producing political pressure to curb expensive overseas assistance and thereby reducing expressed political/diplomatic support for actors in the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::crude_price_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in crude prices feed into inflation and higher interest‑rate expectations, raising cost of capital and causing investors and corporates to pull back or reprioritize funding away from capital‑intensive AI projects and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
