<edge source="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" target="iran_us_regional_war::escalation_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in hostile incidents against energy shipping that are attributed to Iranian forces or allied proxies prompts reciprocal diplomatic pressure, higher alert postures, and threats of retaliatory strikes from the US and partners, directly increasing systemic escalation pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_us_regional_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" target="iran_us_regional_war::military_engagement_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">More frequent attacks on commercial and military escort vessels produces immediate kinetic responses—escort missions, defensive strikes, and interdictions—raising the aggregate rate and intensity of military engagements in the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_us_regional_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" target="market_monetary_stress::market_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in maritime attacks generate abrupt funding and hedging stress (higher margins, insurance and counterparty risk) in short‑dated money and derivatives markets, which translates into higher market‑implied short‑term rate paths as participants price liquidity and risk premia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-3 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">market_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::strike_frequency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising hostile incidents against energy shipping (attacks on tankers, interdictions) provoke retaliatory or pre-emptive military operations by state actors in the theatre, producing an immediate increase in the rate and intensity of kinetic strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shift::attack_incidence_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_control" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in hostile incidents against energy shipping elevates national‑security concerns and political pressure, prompting governments to tighten export controls, licensing and vetting related to AI compute and semiconductor transfers.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
